        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now let me do a final spec compliance check. Let me compare the implementation against every spec requirement:\n\n**Spec 2.1 — `SendStream()` method:** Implemented. Request construction reuses `convertToOpenAIMessages`, `convertToOpenAITools`, same temp/max_tokens logic. Sets `stream: true` and `stream_options: {include_usage: true}`. Non-2xx returns `ProviderError` via `handleErrorResponse`. 2xx wraps body in `EventStream`. Context cancellation returns `ErrCategoryTimeout`.\n\n**Spec 2.2 — SSE-to-StreamEvent mapping:** All mapping rules implemented:\n- `[DONE]` → `io.EOF` (or `StreamEventDone` if no usage chunk)\n- Text content → `StreamEventText`\n- Tool call with `id` → `StreamEventToolStart`\n- Tool call without `id` → `StreamEventToolDelta` (looked up by index)\n- `finish_reason: \"tool_calls\"` → `StreamEventToolEnd` per tool (by ascending index)\n- `finish_reason: \"stop\"/\"length\"` → stored, continue\n- Usage chunk → `StreamEventDone` with tokens\n- Empty delta → skip\n- JSON parse failure → `ProviderError` with `ErrCategoryServer`\n\n**Spec 2.3 — Wire format types:** All structs added with correct JSON tags.\n\n**Spec 2.4 — Edge cases:**\n1. Empty `delta.content` → skipped (tested)\n2. Multiple tool calls in parallel → tracked by index (tested)\n3. Content and tool_calls in same response → both emit correctly\n4. Connection drop mid-stream → wrapped in `ProviderError{ErrCategoryServer}`\n5. Context cancelled mid-stream → `ProviderError{ErrCategoryTimeout}`\n6. No choices in chunk → handled gracefully (usage chunk)\n7. `finish_reason: \"length\"` → treated like stop (tested)\n8. `stream_options` not supported → emits `StreamEventDone` with zero tokens (tested)\n\n**Spec 2.5 — Code reuse:** All specified functions reused without modification.\n\nAll spec requirements are met. Let me commit the changes:",
